# What NOT to deploy.
#
# vercel.json sets `outputDirectory: "."`, so without this file the whole
# repository is published as static content. That is not merely untidy — it
# defeats the point of the project:
#
#   sources/ holds the three original hand-built charts, with every character,
#   relationship and reveal inline and no spoiler gate at all. They were being
#   served at /sources/Empyrean-Chart.html, where anyone could read the ending
#   of a series the live chart carefully withholds. sources/README.md claimed
#   these files "are not served", which was true of nothing but the intent.
#
# Everything the site actually needs is listed at the bottom as an exception,
# so the default is to publish nothing and new directories do not leak by
# simply existing.

# Source, tooling and tests
node_modules
src
tests
scripts
pipeline
evals
mcp
docs
sources
.github
.vercel

# Config and manifests
tsconfig.json
vite.config.ts
vite.chart.config.ts
package.json
package-lock.json

# Working notes and planning docs
BUILD-PLAN.md
UPGRADES.md
DATA-MODEL.md
DATA-REVIEW.md
DATA-DICTIONARY.md
RELATIONSHIPS.md
FILTERS.md
AUTONOMY.md
CHANGELOG.md

# The site itself is what is left: index.html, images/, chart/, data/,
# how-it-works/ and the four *-Chart/ directories. `data/` must ship — the
# chart engine fetches it at runtime — and it is already spoiler-safe, because
# gate() does the withholding at read time rather than at build time.
